/**
 *
 * \defgroup algorithms_group Generic algorithms
 * \ingroup technical_topics_group
 * @{
 *
 * Generic algorithms come in two flavors: approximation schemes/policies
 * (see the Topics below) and a family of graph algorithms genericized via
 * C++20 concepts, detailed in \ref algorithms_graphable "the section below".
 *
 * \section algorithms_graphable Generic graph algorithms via GUM_*Graphable concepts
 *
 * A family of free functions in `gum::graph` (`src/agrum/base/graphs/algorithms/generic/`)
 * is written once and generalized across concrete graph types through four
 * C++20 concepts defined in `graphConcepts.h`: \c GUM_NodeGraphable (base),
 * \c GUM_DiGraphable and \c GUM_UndiGraphable (both refine it), and
 * \c GUM_MixedGraphable (refines both). DiGraph/DAG satisfy GUM_DiGraphable,
 * UndiGraph satisfies GUM_UndiGraphable, MixedGraph/PDAG satisfy
 * GUM_MixedGraphable -- each checked by a compile-time `static_assert`.
 *
 * - <b>Path finding</b> (`pathFinding.h`): directedPath(), hasDirectedPath(),
 *   directedUnorientedPath() on GUM_DiGraphable; undirectedPath(),
 *   hasUndirectedPath() on GUM_UndiGraphable; mixedOrientedPath(),
 *   mixedUnorientedPath() on GUM_MixedGraphable.
 * - <b>Reachability &amp; connectivity</b> (`reachability.h`): ancestors(),
 *   descendants(), family() on GUM_DiGraphable; chainComponents(),
 *   areConnected() on GUM_UndiGraphable; connectedComponents() on the base
 *   GUM_NodeGraphable (dispatches internally via `if constexpr`);
 *   chainComponent(), boundary() on GUM_MixedGraphable.
 * - <b>Topological structure</b> (`cycleDetection.h`): topologicalOrder()
 *   (Kahn's algorithm) on GUM_DiGraphable; hasUndirectedCycle() on
 *   GUM_UndiGraphable.
 * - <b>Causal/probabilistic separation</b> (`separation.h`, `bayesBall.h`,
 *   `moralization.h`): dSeparated() (Bayes Ball) and cSeparated()
 *   (moralization-based, Pearl 1988) on GUM_DiGraphable /
 *   GUM_MixedGraphable, built on requisiteNodes(), dConnected(),
 *   moralGraph() and moralizedAncestralGraph().
 * - <b>Markov blanket</b> (`markovBlanket.h`): markovBlanket() on
 *   GUM_DiGraphable.
 * - <b>Minimal conditioning set</b> (`minimalConditioningSet.h`):
 *   minimalCondSet() on GUM_DiGraphable.
 * - <b>Textual graph construction</b> (`fastGraph.h`): fastGraph() parses a
 *   DOT-like description ("A->B->C; B-E") into any GUM_NodeGraphable graph
 *   type, using GUM_DiGraphable / GUM_UndiGraphable internally to decide
 *   which edge tokens are legal for the requested type.
 *
 * This generalization is currently confined to `src/agrum/base/graphs/`:
 * higher-level modules (BN, MRF, CN, PRM, ...) call these free functions
 * directly rather than constraining their own templates by these concepts.
 *
 *
 * \defgroup approximationscheme_group Approximation Scheme algorithms
 * @{
 * About aGrUM approximation schemes.
 * @}
 * \defgroup approximationpolicy_group Approximation algorithms
 * @{
 * About aGrUM approximation policies.
 * @}
 *
 * @}
 */
